    "question": {
      ":question/id": "ad01de40-9abb-5455-bb1b-3d11f0cc3bd8",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $B,$ given by\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{1}\\leftrightarrow{R}_{3}$ on $B?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The operation ${R}_{1}\\leftrightarrow{R}_{3}$ means that we need to swap the first and third rows.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\quad {R}_{1}\\leftrightarrow{R}_{3} \\\\ & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
