      ":question/id": "8648e562-b5fb-508a-adcb-6a948b3d7b0f",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $C,$ given by\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $C?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}$ means that we need to add $2$ times the second row to the first row.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $1$ times the third row to the first row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\quad {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}1+(2)(4) & 2+(2)(5) & 3+(2)(7) \\\\ 4 & 5 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}9 & 12 & 17 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\quad {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{3} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}9+(1)(-2) & 12+(1)(6) & 17+(1)(8) \\\\ 4 & 5 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}7 & 18 & 25 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
